<% content_for :title, "Installing Ruby" %>

<%= render 'navbar' %>

<section class="guide" id="guide" style="padding-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--pad));">
  <div class="guide__inner">
    <a href="<%= guides_path %>" class="guide__back" data-turbo="false">← All guides</a>
    <h1 class="guide__title">Installing Ruby</h1>
    <p class="guide__lede">
      One recommended path for macOS and Linux: install mise, then use it to install Ruby.
      On Windows, use the official ruby-lang.org instructions linked below.
    </p>

    <div class="guide__body">
      <h2>1. Check for an existing Ruby</h2>
      <p>Run the version check:</p>
      <pre><code>ruby -v</code></pre>
      <p>
        If it prints a recent version, you can stop. If the command is missing or reports an old
        system Ruby, continue with the steps below.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Install mise</h2>
      <p>mise installs and manages Ruby versions for you.</p>
      <pre><code>curl https://mise.run | sh</code></pre>

      <h2>3. Activate mise</h2>
      <p>Add mise to your shell, then restart your terminal. For zsh:</p>
      <pre><code>echo 'eval "$(~/.local/bin/mise activate zsh)"' &gt;&gt; ~/.zshrc</code></pre>
      <p>For bash:</p>
      <pre><code>echo 'eval "$(~/.local/bin/mise activate bash)"' &gt;&gt; ~/.bashrc</code></pre>
      <p>For fish:</p>
      <pre><code>echo '~/.local/bin/mise activate fish | source' &gt;&gt; ~/.config/fish/config.fish</code></pre>

      <h2>4. Install Ruby</h2>
      <p>Install the latest stable Ruby and set it as your default:</p>
      <pre><code>mise use --global ruby@latest</code></pre>
      <p>This can take a few minutes while Ruby compiles.</p>

      <h2>5. Verify the install</h2>
      <pre><code>ruby -v</code></pre>
      <p>
        You should see a recent version, for example <code>ruby 4.0.5</code>. Use the latest stable
        Ruby even if your output shows a newer release.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Troubleshooting</h2>
      <h3>Missing build tools</h3>
      <p>On macOS, install the command line tools:</p>
      <pre><code>xcode-select --install</code></pre>
      <p>On Debian or Ubuntu, install the compiler and Ruby build dependencies:</p>
      <pre><code>sudo apt-get install -y build-essential libssl-dev libyaml-dev libreadline-dev zlib1g-dev libffi-dev</code></pre>

      <h3>OpenSSL mismatch on macOS</h3>
      <p>
        If the Ruby build fails with an OpenSSL error after Homebrew installs a newer OpenSSL,
        build Ruby against <code>openssl@3</code> instead:
      </p>
      <pre><code>brew install openssl@3
RUBY_CONFIGURE_OPTS="--with-openssl-dir=$(brew --prefix openssl@3)" mise install ruby@latest --force</code></pre>

      <h2>7. Other platforms and managers</h2>
      <p>
        For Windows, other platforms, and alternative version managers, see the
        <a href="https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/documentation/installation/">official Ruby installation guide</a>.
        If you already use rbenv, keep using it:
        <a href="https://github.com/rbenv/rbenv#installation">rbenv installation</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Get help</h2>
      <p>
        Stuck? Come to the <a href="<%= events_path %>" data-turbo="false">next Ruby Lang NYC event</a>
        and ask in person.
      </p>
      <!-- Placeholder: replace with the community Slack invite URL. -->
      <p>
        You can also ask questions in the
        <a href="https://join.slack.com/t/rubylangnyc/shared_invite/zt-4evyxc2cl-x4SgFOC486_j_CFHBCZmwg">community Slack</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%= render 'footer' %>

<script nonce="<%= request.content_security_policy_nonce %>">
  (function() {
    const toggle = document.getElementById('navToggle');
    const links  = document.getElementById('navLinks');
    toggle?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      links.classList.toggle('nav__links--open');
      toggle.classList.toggle('nav__toggle--open');
    });

    const moreToggle = document.getElementById('moreToggle');
    const moreMenu   = document.getElementById('moreMenu');
    moreToggle?.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      e.stopPropagation();
      const open = moreMenu.classList.toggle('nav__dropdown-menu--open');
      moreToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open);
    });
    document.addEventListener('click', () => {
      moreMenu?.classList.remove('nav__dropdown-menu--open');
      moreToggle?.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    });

    const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach(e => {
        if (e.isIntersecting) {
          const idx = Array.from(e.target.parentNode.children).indexOf(e.target);
          e.target.style.transitionDelay = `${(idx % 3) * 0.08}s`;
          e.target.classList.add('revealed');
          io.unobserve(e.target);
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.1 });
    document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(c => io.observe(c));
  })()
</script>
